# Lich's Relic in a three-player game: "for each opponent, destroy up to one target creature or planeswalker that player controls".
# The core makes a slot for each opponent; Bot2 and Bot3 each control two Ornithopters. Bot1 picks one of Bot2's and one of
# Bot3's, and each opponent loses exactly one - the other Ornithopters stay. Bot1's turn four is the first with a Black Lotus to pay.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Lich's Relic
Island x5
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Ornithopter
Island x5
Island x12

[Bot3 Deck]
Ornithopter
Ornithopter
Island x5
Island x12

[Actions]
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot3.Main1]
Bot3.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot3.Pass
Bot3.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot3.Pass
[T4 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Black)
Bot1.Hand.Lich's Relic.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot3.Pass
Bot1.PayCost
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter#1)
! Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter#2)
Bot1.Target(Bot3.Battlefield.Ornithopter#1)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot3.Pass

[Expect]
Bot2.Battlefield = Ornithopter
Bot2.Graveyard = Ornithopter
Bot3.Battlefield = Ornithopter
Bot3.Graveyard = Ornithopter
Stack.Count = 0
